:name: CAN PoC step 5: NUCLEO-G431KB FDCAN1 loopback
:description: runs firmware/build/g431_loopback.elf on renode/stm32g431kb.repl (which has FDCAN1). a CANHub with loopback on echoes every frame back, standing in for the FDCAN internal loopback mode that Renode doesn't model.
:
: how to run (from the top folder, the one with firmware/ and renode/):
:   make -C firmware
:   renode renode/g431_loopback.resc then type: start
:   expected --> the FDCAN clock and bit rate read back from the registers,
:   then 20 lines "FDCAN1 loopback RX id=0x100 ... OK" and "LOOPBACK PASS"
:
: external loopback build (acts the same in Renode, on hardware it also
: drives PA12) --> set $elf before including this script:
:   $elf=@firmware/build/g431_ext_loopback.elf
:   include @renode/g431_loopback.resc

using sysbus
$name?="g431"
mach create $name
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/stm32g431kb.repl

$elf?=@firmware/build/g431_loopback.elf
macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $elf
    cpu VectorTableOffset 0x08000000
"""
runMacro $reset

# Renode workaround: the FDCAN model ignores TEST.LBCK, so the chip can't hear
# itself. a hub made with loopback = true sends every frame back to the
# controller that sent it --> same result as the real loopback
emulation CreateCANHub "loop" true
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 loop

showAnalyzer usart2

include @renode/art/g431_loopback.py
